      "text": "### ADF Data Flows ARE Spark"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#003",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
        "canonical_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "current_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "id": "maxim:query-languages:sparksql",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "query-languages",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "If you've built ADF Data Flows, you've been writing Spark SQL without knowing it. Data Flows are a visual canvas that compiles to a Spark execution plan. The Azure Integration Runtime that runs them is a Spark cluster managed by Microsoft. Every transformation you've dragged onto the canvas generates Spark code:"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#004",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
        "canonical_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "current_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "id": "maxim:query-languages:sparksql",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "query-languages",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nADF Data Flow Canvas → Spark Execution Plan\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nADF Transformation    │ Spark DataFrame API     │ Spark SQL equivalent\n──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────\nSelect (column pick)  │ .select(\"col1\",\"col2\")  │ SELECT col1, col2 FROM ...\nFilter                │ .filter(col > 5)         │ WHERE col > 5\nAggregate             │ .groupBy().agg()         │ GROUP BY + aggregates\nJoin                  │ .join(other, key, type)  │ JOIN ... ON ...\nSort                  │ .orderBy(col.desc())     │ ORDER BY col DESC\nDerived Column        │ .withColumn(\"c\", expr)  │ SELECT *, expr AS c\nConditional Split     │ .filter() per branch     │ multiple WHERE clauses\nFlatten               │ .select(explode(...))    │ LATERAL VIEW EXPLODE\nLookup                │ .join(..., \"left\")        │ LEFT JOIN\nExists                │ .join(..., \"left_semi\")   │ WHERE EXISTS (subquery)\nWindow                │ .withColumn(win_fn)      │ OVER (PARTITION BY ...)\nPivot                 │ .groupBy().pivot().agg() │ PIVOT\nUnpivot               │ stack() expression       │ UNPIVOT / UNION ALL\nRank                  │ .withColumn(rank_fn)     │ ROW_NUMBER() OVER (...)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#005",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
