        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Synapse Analytics is the Azure-managed environment that hosts Spark alongside other compute options:"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#009",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
        "canonical_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "current_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "id": "maxim:query-languages:sparksql",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "query-languages",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nAzure Synapse Analytics workspace\n├── Spark pools              ← the same Apache Spark runtime described in this guide\n│   └── Attach notebooks, Synapse pipelines, or trigger via REST\n├── Dedicated SQL pool       ← MPP data warehouse (T-SQL, column store, separate from Spark)\n├── Serverless SQL pool      ← query Delta/Parquet in ADLS with T-SQL via OPENROWSET\n└── Data Explorer pool       ← time-series and log analytics (KQL)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#010",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
        "canonical_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "current_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "id": "maxim:query-languages:sparksql",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "query-languages",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Spark pools in Synapse run the same Spark runtime. Spark SQL queries, DataFrames, MLlib, Structured Streaming — all covered in this guide — run identically in a Synapse Spark pool and a Databricks cluster. The difference is the management surface: Synapse is more Azure-native (AAD, ADLS Gen2 managed identity, Synapse Studio UI); Databricks adds Unity Catalog, Delta Live Tables, MLflow, and a richer notebook experience."
    },
    {
