        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SQL Server's query optimizer works on a query tree — a hierarchical plan where each node has one parent. Catalyst works on a DAG (Directed Acyclic Graph) of transformations. The distinction matters when multiple branches of a query share a common sub-expression: Catalyst can represent that sub-expression once and pipe its output to multiple consumers without recomputing it."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#018",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
        "canonical_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "current_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "id": "maxim:query-languages:sparksql",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "query-languages",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCatalyst pipeline (4 phases):"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#019",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
        "canonical_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "current_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "id": "maxim:query-languages:sparksql",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "query-languages",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SQL string / DataFrame API\n         │\n         ▼\n  1. Parse → Unresolved Logical Plan (AST: no column types, no table validation)\n         │\n         ▼\n  2. Analyze → Resolved Logical Plan (column types resolved, tables validated against catalog)\n         │\n         ▼\n  3. Optimize → Optimized Logical Plan\n         │   Rule-based:  predicate pushdown, column pruning, constant folding,\n         │               subquery elimination, NULL propagation\n         │   Cost-based:  join reordering based on table statistics (if available)\n         ▼\n  4. Physical Planning → one or more Physical Plans (SparkPlan)\n         │   Strategies: BroadcastHashJoin vs SortMergeJoin vs ShuffleHashJoin\n         │   Selected via cost model\n         ▼\n  5. Code Generation (Tungsten / WholeStageCodegen)\n         │   Generates JVM bytecode per stage — not interpreted row-by-row\n         │   LLVM-style loop fusion: multiple operators collapse into one tight loop\n         ▼\n  Execution (RDD partitions → tasks → executors)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#020",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
        "canonical_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "current_path": "query-languages/08-SPARKSQL.md",
        "id": "maxim:query-languages:sparksql",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "query-languages",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[sparksql]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Spark SQL + Delta Lake",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SQL Server bridge: SQL Server's optimizer does predicate pushdown and hash join selection too. The difference is Spark's plan is a DAG (shared sub-expressions) while SQL Server's is a tree. Spark's code generation (Tungsten) is Spark's equivalent of SQL Server's batch mode execution on columnstore — vectorized, tight loops, not row-by-row operator evaluation."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-SPARKSQL.md#021",
      "path": [
        "08-SPARKSQL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:08-sparksql, git-history:query-languages:08-sparksql]",
